romanized_response:
HTTP status code 429 Too Many Requests andre server nalli yavudo rate limit ide mattu nimma request adannu exceed madide anta artha. Idu kelagina yavudadaru karanagalinda agirabahudu:

1. Ee request maduva code annu swalpa samayadalli tumba sala run madirabahudu, adarinda rate limit exceed agirabahudu.

2. Website spam anta suspect maduva requests annu 429 status code jothe reject madutte. Idara artha user agent common browser agirade irabahudu, idu kelavu websites use maduva simple check. Idannu sari madalu, GET request ge "User-Agent" header annu heege add madabahudu:

```
const response = await axios.get('https://www.realestate.com.au/rent/in-sydney,+nsw/list-1', 
     { headers: { 'User-Agent': 'browser.version' }  }
);
```

`"browser.version"` annu nijavada browser user agent string inda replace madabeku annodannu gamanisi. Ee code yavva application nalli run aguttide annodara mele, idannu user agent spoofing anta pariganisabahudu, mattu kelavu deshagalu athava organizations gala laws adiyalli restrict agirabahudu (athava code access madalu try maduva website na terms of service adiyalli restrict agirabahudu).

3. Website bere yavudo karanakke requests ge rate limit maduttirabahudu. Idu request proxy moolaka maduttiruvudinda agirabahudu; anthaha case nalli proxy ya bere users tumba requests madirabahudu, adare idu sambhavane kadime.

4. Website denial of service attack adiyalli iruvudinda ella requests annu reject maduttirabahudu. Idu sambhavane kadime, ekendare anthaha attack adiyalli server na typical behavior traffic annu non-existent server ge route maduvudu, athava adannu completely deny maduvudu, adarinda valid response yenu sigalla. Adare, website HTTP status code jothe respond madidaroo, server overloaded agiruvaga koduva server error 503 Service Unavailable baruva sadhyate hecchu.

response_en:
Yes, certainly! The issue you're encountering is because the string literals "fizzbuzz", "fizz", and "buzz" are temporary values, and you are trying to return a reference to them, which is not allowed because they will be dropped at the end of the scope, and the returned reference would be dangling.

You can fix this error by returning &'static str instead of &str. &'static str refers to string literals, which have a 'static lifetime, meaning they last for the duration of the program. Here's an updated version of your code:

fn fizzbuzz(n: usize) -> &'static str {
    match (n % 3, n % 5) {
        (0, 0) => "fizzbuzz",
        (0, _) => "fizz",
        (_, 0) => "buzz",
        _ => {
            let s = n.to_string();
            Box::leak(s.into_boxed_str())
        }
    }
}

Note that the last arm returns a &'static str that is created from a String using the Box::leak function, which takes ownership of a Box<T> and returns a pointer to its contents, effectively leaking it. This is safe because the returned pointer will last for the duration of the program, but it should be used with care as it will not be cleaned up automatically.

romanized_response:
Haudu, khandita! Neevu edurisuttiruva issue yaakandre "fizzbuzz", "fizz", mattu "buzz" string literals temporary values aagive, mattu neevu avugalige reference return maadalu try maaduttiddira. Adu allowed alla, yaakandre scope konege avu drop aaguttave, mattu return aada reference dangling aaguttade.

Ee error fix maadalu &str badalige &'static str return maadabahudu. &'static str string literals ge refer maaduttade, avugalige 'static lifetime iruttade, andare program na duration poorthi avu iruttave. Nimma code na updated version illide:

fn fizzbuzz(n: usize) -> &'static str {
    match (n % 3, n % 5) {
        (0, 0) => "fizzbuzz",
        (0, _) => "fizz",
        (_, 0) => "buzz",
        _ => {
            let s = n.to_string();
            Box::leak(s.into_boxed_str())
        }
    }
}

Note maadi, last arm &'static str return maaduttade; adu Box::leak function use maadi String inda create maadida value. Ee function Box<T> na ownership tegedukondu adara contents ge pointer return maaduttade, effectively adannu leak maaduttade. Idu safe, yaakandre return aada pointer program na duration poorthi iruttade, aadre idannu care inda use maadabeku, yaakandre idu automatically clean up aaguvudilla.

response_en:
Merge sort is a divide and conquer algorithm that works by recursively splitting the input array in half until the arrays are split into single elements. Then, the sorted arrays are merged back together in sorted order.

The key benefits of merge sort over a simpler algorithm like bubble sort are:

1. It is a stable sort that does not change the relative order of elements with equal keys.
2. It has an efficiency of O(n log n) time complexity, making it a relatively efficient algorithm even for large input sizes. Bubble sort, on the other hand, has a quadratic time complexity of O(n^2), making it very inefficient for larger inputs.
3. It is a generic algorithm that can sort any type of data for which a comparison function exists.

Here is a Rust implementation example:
```rust
fn merge_sort(vec: &mut [i32]) {
    if vec.len() < 2 {
        return;
    }

    let mid = vec.len() / 2;
    let (left, right) = vec.split_at_mut(mid);

    merge_sort(left);
    merge_sort(right);

    merge(left, right, vec);
}

fn merge(left: &mut [i32], right: &mut [i32], vec: &mut [i32]) {
    let mut i = 0;
    let mut j = 0;
    let mut k = 0;

    while i < left.len() && j < right.len() {
        if left[i] < right[j] {
            vec[k] = left[i];
            i += 1;
        } else {
            vec[k] = right[j];
            j += 1;
        }
        k += 1;
    }

    while i < left.len() {
        vec[k] = left[i];
        i += 1;
        k += 1;
    }

    while j < right.len() {
        vec[k] = right[j];
        j += 1;
        k += 1;
    }
}
```

romanized_response:
Merge sort ondu divide and conquer algorithm. Idu input array annu recursively half aagi split madutta, arrays single elements aagi split aaguvavarege kelasa madutte. Aamele, sorted arrays annu sorted order nalli matte merge madalagutte.

Bubble sort antha simple algorithm ge compare madidare merge sort na mukhya benefits ivu:

1. Idu stable sort; equal keys iruva elements na relative order annu change madalla.
2. Idara efficiency O(n log n) time complexity, adarinda large input sizes ge kooda idu relatively efficient algorithm. Innondede, bubble sort ge O(n^2) antha quadratic time complexity ide, adarinda larger inputs ge adu tumba inefficient.
3. Idu generic algorithm; comparison function iruva yava type of data annadaru sort madabahudu.

Illi ondu Rust implementation example ide:
```rust
